Subject: [PATCH] fix: 6 real bugs found in feature audit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Username login (CRITICAL): RPC fix didn't apply on Windows sed — auth.js
   still queried profiles table directly, blocked by RLS for unauthenticated
   users. Now correctly uses rpc('get_email_by_username') SECURITY DEFINER fn.

2. Vision fallback model deprecated: VISION_FALLBACK was 'llama-3.2-11b-vision-preview'
   which Groq retired in late 2024. Every vision failure silently failed on the
   fallback too. Updated to 'llama-3.2-11b-vision-instruct' (stable).

3. Supabase init crash: createClient('','') throws 'supabaseUrl is required'
   when Vercel env vars are missing (caused the May 22 Sentry incident). Now
   guards with an explicit check and logs a clear error instead of crashing.

4. Referral bonus bypass: localStorage.removeItem('hs_used_ref') let users
   claim 10 bonus scans unlimited times. Now also writes to referral_claims
   table (server-side) so the claim is persisted even if localStorage is cleared.
   Added referral_claims table + RLS to migration SQL.

5. HUNT_DATA stale prices: India prices were 2024 estimates, now updated to
   2025 market values (+10-20% across the board). Added 3 missing popular
   castings: Bone Shaker, '67 Camaro, RWB Porsche 930.

6. groqVision no timeout: Vision calls had no hard timeout — a hung Groq
   request would freeze the UI forever. Added 30s Promise.race timeout with
   a user-friendly error message.
